WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.129
When it comes to the Sith, the big bad villains
of the Star Wars universe, there's more than

00:00:05.129 --> 00:00:07.229
one way to skin a Jedi.

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:12.410
Some Sith were strong in the force, while
others wielded sinister magic, or huge political

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:13.410
influence.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.629
So who comes out on top when you add it all
up?

00:00:15.629 --> 00:00:18.540
Here are the most powerful Sith ever...

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.630
Freedon Nadd

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:23.949
Freedon Nadd was a Jedi in the days of the
Old Republic, with Force talents far beyond

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:25.450
any of his peers.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:30.289
While training, he became jealous of his Jedi
master's power and authority, so in true Sith

00:00:30.289 --> 00:00:36.120
fashion, he killed him and renounced his affiliation
with the Jedi — man, what a baby.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.250
"I hate you"

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.621
Nadd was trained in the ways of the Dark Side
by Naga Sadow (nahguh s’dao), a Sith lord

00:00:41.621 --> 00:00:42.730
living in exile.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:48.080
After his death, Freedon Nadd's ghost continued
to manipulate events from beyond the grave.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.800
Marka Ragnos (Ragnus)

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.900
Marka Ragnos was a Sith Lord who grew tired
of the Sith's unwillingness to expand beyond

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.790
their homeworld of Korriban (Korrabun).

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:59.960
His reign was ruthless and brutal, but most
of the time, he achieved victory without raising

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:00.960
a finger.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.440
A master of manipulation, Ragnos set his adversaries
against one another, using their mutually

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.280
assured destruction to clear an easy path
for the Sith.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.920
And his story didn't end with his death either:
as a Force ghost, he pitted Sith Lords against

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:16.310
each other for the honor of becoming the official
Dark Lord.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:21.070
"You will kneel before me, Jedi."

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:22.070
Darth Bane

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:26.260
Darth Bane is the Star Wars expanded universe's
version of a Founding Father when it comes

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.100
to the Dark Side of the Force.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:33.270
As the last surviving member of the Sith Brotherhood
of Darkness, Bane started a new Sith Order,

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:37.742
and decided to pass his knowledge onto a single
apprentice, establishing the Rule of Two that

00:01:37.742 --> 00:01:39.900
the Sith Lords have followed ever since.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:45.260
"The Sith killed each other, victims of their
own greed.

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:51.690
But from the ashes of destruction I
was the last survivor.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:57.060
I chose to pass my knowledge on to only one."

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.600
Darth Vader

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:02.549
As Anakin Skywalker, the man who would become
Darth Vader was expected to become the most

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:07.420
powerful Force user of all time, as he had
the highest midi-chlorian count ever recorded.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:11.080
"I heard Yoda talking about midi-chlorians.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:14.740
I've been wondering, what are midi-chlorians?"

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.820
Uhhh, let's not get into that.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:21.200
But anyway, after massacring the students
of the Jedi Academy, Anakin was severely wounded

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.280
by his master Obi-Wan Kenobi, and as the cyborg
Vader, he lost some of his connection to the

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.280
Force.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:32.340
Still, he had perhaps the most impressive
power of all: terrifying generations of moviegoers.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:37.020
"I find your lack of faith disturbing."

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.520
Darth Nihilus (Nigh-h’luss)

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.690
The Dark Side of the Force can be seen as
a metaphor for addiction.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.209
Darth Nihilus offers a perfect example.

00:02:44.209 --> 00:02:48.290
After he was caught in the detonation of the
super-weapon known as the Mass Shadow Generator,

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:52.490
which destroyed the planet Malachor V (five),
Nihilus' body was wrecked.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:56.400
He was left with an insatiable craving for
Force energy — essentially turning him into

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.800
a Force vampire.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:58.800
Yikes.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.790
Revan (Revvin)

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:04.300
Like so many other Sith, Revan also started
as a Jedi.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:08.420
He turned to the Dark Side after the Jedi
Council refused to protect the lives of Outer

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.090
Rim innocents caught in the Mandalorian Wars.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:15.260
Over their objections, Revan assembled at
large Jedi defense team, helping the Republic

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:18.489
win the war, but leading him down the dark
path to corruption.

00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:21.849
He eventually embraced the light side again
and helped defeat the Sith.

00:03:21.849 --> 00:03:26.560
"I've known both sides of the force, light
and dark."

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.260
Darth Sidious

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:33.250
Better known to most fans as Emperor Palpatine,
Darth Sidious rose to power thanks to ruthless

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:34.250
cunning.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.790
After murdering his master, Darth Plagueis
(Playgus) , the Emperor hid in plain sight

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.200
as the benevolent galactic senator from Naboo.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.430
Secretly orchestrating the Clone Wars, which
allowed him to consolidate political power,

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:49.660
Darth Sidious corrupted Anakin Skywalker and
virtually wiped the Jedi out of existence,

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:53.349
turning the tables after thousands of years
of Jedi dominance over the Sith.

00:03:53.349 --> 00:04:04.069
"I'm afraid the deflector shield will be quite
operational when your friends arrive."

00:04:04.069 --> 00:04:05.560
Darth Plagueis

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:10.340
Darth Plagueis wasn't the most skilled Force
user, nor was he a military leader, or particularly

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:11.849
good with a lightsaber.

00:04:11.849 --> 00:04:16.160
Instead, Plagueis was a scholar and a scientist,
who focused his scholarly efforts on a single

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:20.849
pursuit: how to manipulate the Force and midi-chlorians
in a way that would allow him to live forever

00:04:20.849 --> 00:04:23.590
and possibly even bring the dead back to life.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:32.699
"Darth Plagueis was a dark lord of the Sith
so powerful and so wise that he could use the

00:04:32.699 --> 00:04:40.219
force to influence the midi-chlorians to create
life."

00:04:40.219 --> 00:04:45.330
With control over life itself, Plagueis feared
only one thing: losing his power.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:48.789
Which he did when his apprentice, Darth Sidious,
killed him in his sleep.

00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:52.830
Some fans theorize, however, that Plagueis
has returned in Star Wars: The Force Awakens

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.879
as the evil Sith lord Snoke.

00:04:54.879 --> 00:04:57.099
Sounds like bad news for Rey!

00:04:57.099 --> 00:05:02.370
"Bring her to me."

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.580
Darth Vitiate (Vishit)

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:07.289
The original Emperor, Darth Vitiate tricked
the other Sith Lords into helping him perform

00:05:07.289 --> 00:05:11.169
a ritual that allowed him to absorb the life
force of every other living being on his home

00:05:11.169 --> 00:05:12.169
planet.

00:05:12.169 --> 00:05:16.710
The ritual granted Vitiate immortality and
immense power, which he used to found a galaxy-spanning

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:20.860
Sith Empire, ruling it with an iron fist for
1300 years.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:27.300
"I have forged this empire to surmount all
of my previous works.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.560
To span eternity."

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:34.780
Yeah, Palpatine had his moments for a few
decades, but when it comes to Sith Emperor's,

00:05:34.789 --> 00:05:35.800
there's really no contest.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:39.410
You can't beat a dude with 1300 years under
his belt…

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:45.389
"I am awakened and I bring with me, death."

00:05:45.389 --> 00:05:46.389
Thanks for watching!

00:05:46.389 --> 00:05:49.279
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:49.279 --> 00:05:52.549
And leave us a comment to let us know which
sith lord you think is the most powerful ever…

